  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rajkumar Yadav @ Rajesh Yadav vs State Of U.P. on 20 May, 2020 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ? In Chamber Case :- Criminal Misc. Bail Application No. - 12751 of 2020 Applicant :- Rajkumar Yadav @ Rajesh Yadav Opposite Party :- State of U.P. Counsel for Applicant :- Prakhar Saran Srivastava Counsel for Opposite Party :- G.A. Hon'ble Siddharth,J.",
    "facts": "Submission is that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 has been enacted by the legislature and hence the implication of the applicant under section 272 I.P.C. is unjustified. Offence under section 60 and 63 of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged.",
    "arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case Rajkumar Yadav @ Rajesh Yadav vs State Of U.P. on 20 May, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/108625852/ 1 of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, the Court is of the view that the applicant has made out a case for bail.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case Rajkumar Yadav @ Rajesh Yadav vs State Of U.P. on 20 May, 2020 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/108625852/ 1 of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22 and without expressing any opinion on the merits of the case, the Court is of the view that the applicant has made out a case for bail."
  },
